  "name": "Alaskan Heavyweights: Bull Walruses of Round Island",
  "description": "The popular place to spend the summer, if you're a walrus, is a tiny island with a few rocky beaches. No wonder there's lot of pushing and shoving. A photographic essay of walruses on Round Island, Bristol Bay, Alaska. [Reference: Hansen, Paul G. 1979. Alaskan heavyweights: Bull walruses of Round Island. Pacific Search Vol. 13 No. 5. pp.5-7.] This volume may be found at many university libraries.\n\nDeposited content: descriptive metadata only; underlying research data are not included.\n\nPurpose: A report on bull walruses of Round Island, Alaska.",
  "url": "https://zenodo.org/records/23563967",
